        "title": "[Feature] Provide connection age-limit warnings before forced WebSocket closure in provider adapters",
        "body": "The WebSocket manager closes cached connections older than a specific age limit (connection_age_limit). However, if the socket is closed while a stream transaction is active or about to start, it results in unexpected connection abort errors for the user.\n\nProposed Solution:\nImplement a soft age limit where connections are flagged as deprecated but kept open to drain active transactions, and raise warning hooks or allow a grace period for pending streams before initiating the forced socket closure.\n\nSource Reference:\npackages/ai/src/providers/openai-chatgpt-responses.ts#L1230-L1235",
